;;     with no all-types entry. Adding the entry the decompiler itself
;;     suggests, (function font-context none) (jak3 carries exactly that),
;;     was tried in scratch: it trades the missing-type error for "Failed to
;;     guess label use for L172 in draw-debug-text-box:3" and still emits an
;;     untyped body. Reverted.
;;   hyphenate-word       same missing-type error; a bare (define-extern
;;     hyphenate-word function) was tried in scratch and changed nothing, so
;;     there is no signature to land it against. Reverted.
;;   print-game-text      six real errors, four of them unsupported inline
;;     assembly (sllv v1, v0, r0), which no config change can reach.
;; The print-game-text-work type and its method 3 stay unlanded with them:
;; the type is declared by this object's own top level via (type-new
;; 'print-game-text-work structure ...) and print-game-text, its only
;; consumer, is the function that would reveal the field layout. The
;; top-level (method-set! (the-as type print-game-text-work) 3 L183) and the
;; (define *print-game-text-work* <static-data L171>) that follow it are held
;; with the type, since both name it.

